Type-collision resolution (no silent drift): the KMP-free EnergyFlow widgets already own
`EnergyDailyEntry`, `EnergyFlowArrow`, and `EnergyFlowFormat` in the same module. The page
types were uniquely renamed to `EnergyFlowDailyEntry`, `EnergyFlowDiagramArrow`, and
`EnergyFlowDisplayFormat` (file renamed to match) so the surface compiles collision-free.

Data sources (web parity):
  - useEnergyFlow            -> GET /vehicles/{id}/energy/flow   (live diagram; kW/kWh/% verbatim)
  - inline energy-stats query-> GET /vehicles/{id}/energy?days=N (historical aggregate; SI Wh/m)
                               -> drives the page phase (web isLoading=statsLoading), the live
                               flow is supplementary (web `?.`) and never gates the page.
  Both bound through EnergyFlowPageModel (@Observable; no networking in the view, ADR-004).
SI discipline (ADR-005): the aggregate stays SI (energy Wh, distance m, efficiency Wh/m) and
  converts at the render boundary via the shared Units facade + EnergyFlowDisplayFormat. The
  live /energy/flow endpoint serves display-scaled kW/kWh/% which render verbatim (web parity).
  Note: the web daily charts plot raw SI while labeling the user's unit; this port converts at
  the boundary (ADR-005) so the bars match their labeled unit and the metric cards (disclosed).

